  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) R.C. 3505.18(A)(1)\n(quote) When an elector appears in a polling place to vote, the elector shall announce to the precinct election officials the elector's full name and current address and provide proof of the elector's identity in the form of a current and valid photo identification, a military identification, a United States passport, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document ... that shows the name and current address of the elector.\n(section) R.C. 3509.051(A)\n(quote) The absent voter shall provide identification to the election officials in the same manner as a voter who casts a ballot in person on the day of an election is required to provide identification under section 3505.18 of the Revised Code.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) R.C. 3505.18(A)(2)\n(quote) If an elector has but is unable to provide to the precinct election officials any of the forms of identification required under division (A)(1) of this section, but has a social security number, the elector may provide the last four digits of the elector's social security number. Upon providing the social security number information, the elector may cast a provisional ballot under section 3505.181 of the Revised Code, the envelope of which ballot shall include that social security number information.\n(section) R.C. 3505.18(A)(5)\n(quote) If an elector executes an affirmation under division (A)(3) of this section stating that the elector does not have any of the forms of identification required under division (A)(1) of this section and, in verifying the elector's eligibility to vote, the election officials determine that the elector does have one of those forms of identification and failed to provide such identification, that elector shall be deemed to have committed election falsification in violation of section 3599.36 of the Revised Code by filing that affirmation and that elector's provisional ballot shall not be counted.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) R.C. 3509.05(A)\n(quote) the elector also shall include in the return envelope with the identification envelope a copy of the elector's current valid photo identification, a copy of a military identification, a copy of a United States passport, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document ... that shows the name and address of the elector.\n(section) R.C. 3509.03(E)\n(quote) One of the following: ... (3) A copy of the elector's current and valid photo identification, a copy of a military identification, a copy of a United States passport, or a copy of a current utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document ...\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) R.C. 3503.20(A)\n(quote) The secretary of state, by rule, shall establish a secure online process for voter registration. The rules shall provide for all of the following: (1) An applicant to submit a voter registration application to the secretary of state online through the internet;\n(other) Same omnibus as H.B. 194 (2011): R.C. 3501.xx boards of elections, bulk purchases (3501.302), contracts between boards (3501.111), suits against election officials (3501.40)\n(other) R.C. 3503.xx: registration (incomplete application notice 3503.05; online registration 3503.20; acknowledgment notices 3503.22); 3504.01 former-elector presidential ballot\n(other) R.C. 3505.xx: polling place and provisional ballots (3505.181-.183); 3505.05 local issue removal; 3506.021 electronic pollbooks\n(other) R.C. 3509.xx / 3511.xx: absentee and uniformed/overseas voting; in-person absentee (3509.051)\n(other) R.C. 3513.xx, 3515.04, 3517.xx, 3519.xx, 3599.xx: primaries, recounts, campaign finance (3517.211), petitions, election offenses\n(other) R.C. 4301.32, 4301.334, 4303.29, 4305.14: liquor local option / permit sections touched\n(other) version: 00_IN: omnibus election bill; polling-place ID list (photo ID, military ID, utility bill etc.); no passport option in the introduced text\n(other) version: 01_RS: adds a United States passport to ID lists (3505.18, 3509.03, 3509.05, 3503.19); keeps SSN-4 provisional rule\n(other) version: 02_PS: same ID text as 01_RS; adds in 3505.18(A)(5) that a person who files a false no-ID affirmation is deemed to have committed election falsification and the provisional ballot is not counted (this wording is in 00_IN vs 02_PS comparison; I could not isolate the version that added it)\n(other) note: 2011 PDF text: struck and new words are not marked, so I cannot tell which of the quoted ID wording is new and which is existing law. The passport addition is the clear change I could detect by comparing versions. The bill passed the Senate only (last version 02_PS). Section summaries come from the long title; the bill parallels H.B. 194. Vote mapping per brief: Senate passage on 01_RS. The six table-amendment votes are on floor amendments whose text I do not have.",
